-- title:
--   Commute GHalf Sandwich Move Chain Lift Move Family Last
-- statement:
--   **Self-consistency closes the lifted move-family endpoint.**
--
--   Let $(m,q,d)$ have a field model, let $\psi_{AB}$ be a bipartite quantum state, let $F$ be a slice-indexed polynomial family, let $\zeta$ be an error parameter, and let $r\in\mathbb N$. Assume that the two completed slice measurement families are $\operatorname{SDDRel}$-related under the uniform slice-question distribution with error
--
--   $$
--   E_{\mathrm{sc}}=2\zeta.
--   $$
--
--   Let $\mathsf M_r$ be the move family with two distinguished completed effects on the left register and the reversed tail half-product on the right. The lifted endpoint and the next move family satisfy
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi_{AB},\,\operatorname{Unif}(\mathsf{MoveQ}_{r+1})}
--   \left(\mathsf L_r(F,\mathsf M_r),\mathsf M_{r+1};E_{\mathrm{sc}}\right).
--   $$
--
--   This is the final comparison that closes the recursive move-chain lift.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.commuteGHalfSandwich_moveChainLift_moveFamily_last`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
